## NOTICE — what the license above does and does not cover

The MIT license above covers the **original work in this repository**:

- the card artwork and board layouts authored for Beta Theta Pi
- the `btp` symbol and footprint library in `lib/`
- the PNM rush schedule card in `pnm-card/`, in its entirety
- the documentation written for this archive (`README.md`, `CLAUDE.md`,
  every file in `docs/` **except** those listed below)

### Not covered: upstream material

`brother-card/` is a fork of
[Raziz1/PCB_Business_Card](https://github.com/Raziz1/PCB_Business_Card) by
**Rahim Aziz**, at commit `fe6c083`. The following are **his work**, reproduced
here with attribution but **not** licensed by the terms above:

- `docs/nfc-theory.md` — his project README, verbatim
- `docs/images/` — his figures, photographs, and simulation screenshots
- `docs/antenna-simulations/` — his LTSpice and MATLAB work
- `docs/renders/upstream-blender/` — his Blender model of his own card
- the antenna geometry, matching-network derivation, and hardware
  characterization that the brother card inherits unchanged

The upstream repository carries **no license file**, so absent an explicit grant
its author retains all rights. That material is included here because this
repository is a fork of his project and because the derivation is what makes the
antenna comprehensible — not as a claim of ownership. See
[`docs/OPEN-QUESTIONS.md`](./docs/OPEN-QUESTIONS.md) §9; obtaining an explicit
license grant from Rahim Aziz is an open item.

If you are Rahim Aziz and would like any of the above removed or relicensed,
please open an issue and it will be handled promptly.

### Not covered: third-party reference documents

`docs/reference/` contains application notes redistributed by their original
publishers — NXP (`AN11276`, dynamic NFC antenna design guide) and
STMicroelectronics (`AN2972`). These remain the property of their respective
publishers and are included for convenience. Prefer the vendors' own copies as
canonical.

### Not covered: Beta Theta Pi insignia

The Beta Theta Pi crest, dragon, `BETA THETA PI` wordmark, and `MEN OF PRINCIPLE`
motto are marks of the **Beta Theta Pi Fraternity**. The MIT license above applies
to this repository's files, not to the fraternity's marks. Reproducing the insignia
requires the fraternity's permission independently of anything granted here.
